BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Timeless Traditions- OSFL's Annual Holiday Concert
DTSTART:20261212T200000Z
DTEND:20261213T045959Z
DTSTAMP:20261128T172939Z
UID:8d09124397b8bca597f6c7dece911b30f12a91fa@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Holidays,Music,Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:Event by The Orchestra of the Southern Finger Lakes\nClemens C
 enter\nPublic\nCelebrate the season with an afternoon of beloved tradition
 s\, beautiful voices\, and plenty of opportunities to join in the music yo
 urself. The Orchestra and Chorus of the Southern Finger Lakes come togethe
 r for a holiday concert designed to feel less like a performance you simpl
 y watch and more like a celebration we create together.\nThe program bring
 s together sacred favorites and timeless holiday music\, from the warmth o
 f O Tannenbaum to three cherished works by John Rutter — Angel Carol\, W
 hat Sweeter Music and Jesus Child. Enjoy Ave Maria by Bach/Gounod before o
 rchestra and chorus join forces for one of the most exhilarating moments i
 n holiday music: Handel's triumphant Hallelujah Chorus from Messiah.\nDisc
 over something new with a world premiere of a new work by Avner Finberg\, 
 and let the orchestra sweep you into the magical world of Tchaikovsky's Th
 e Nutcracker with the elegant Pas de deux and dazzling Waltz of the Flower
 s.\nAfter intermission\, it's your turn to join in. Two Christmas Pops Sin
 g-Alongs fill the hall with favorites including Santa Claus Is Comin' to T
 own\, Rudolph\, White Christmas\, Winter Wonderland\, Let It Snow\, Jingle
  Bell Rock and The Christmas Song. Along the way\, enjoy the serene beauty
  of Vaughan Williams' Fantasia on Greensleeves and the traditional All Thr
 ough the Night before raising your voice once more for a Christmas carol s
 ing-along.\nAnd no OSFL holiday celebration would be complete without one 
 final tradition: Anderson's unmistakable Sleigh Ride.\nWhether these songs
  have been part of your holidays for decades or you're experiencing them w
 ith us for the first time\, come ready to listen\, sing\, celebrate\, and 
 share in the joy of making music together.\nFun for the whole family\, kid
 s under 18 are free with an adult ticket purchase.\nTickets: https://cleme
 nscenter.org/event/orchestra-of-the-southern-finger-lakes-presents-timeles
 s-traditions/?fbclid=IwY2xjawVpeZVleHRuA2FlbQIxMABwZG9mBXNydGMGYXBwX2lkEDI
 yMjAzOTE3ODgyMDA4OTIAAR9HmhBvgqDt7bG2247bI0vhySiXM7u71lKwJCNXi33fuvXk2LFyX
 DeyXVrwMQ_aem_jrJdkkNIvESnAh2P1O5QxA.\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://cal
 endar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78518650/20261212150000
GEO:42.08921;-76.804956
LOCATION:Clemens Center\, 207 Clemens Center Parkway\, Elmira\, New York\,
  14901
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://clemenscenter.org/event/orchestra-of-the-southern-finger-lakes
 -presents-timeless-traditions/?fbclid=IwY2xjawVpeZVleHRuA2FlbQIxMABwZG9mBX
 NydGMGYXBwX2lkEDIyMjAzOTE3ODgyMDA4OTIAAR9HmhBvgqDt7bG2247bI0vhySiXM7u71lKw
